# The dummy application's test database.
#
# `db/*.sqlite3` above does not reach it: a pattern containing a slash is anchored to the
# directory holding the .gitignore, so that one matches only the repo root's db/.  `log/` has no
# slash and so already matches a log directory at any depth, including test/dummy/log -- those
# files were reported as modified only because they were already tracked, and .gitignore never
# applies to a tracked path.  Hence the `git rm --cached` alongside this.
test/dummy/db/*.sqlite3
